WEBVTT

00:00.400 --> 00:03.899
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.900 --> 00:07.204
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.205 --> 00:10.777
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.778 --> 00:13.783
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.784 --> 00:17.289
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.290 --> 00:20.629
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.630 --> 00:22.165
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.166 --> 00:24.068
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.069 --> 00:28.746
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.087 --> 00:35.422
We now return to

00:35.423 --> 00:37.927
<i>How David Lynch Stole Christmas.</i>

00:39.564 --> 00:42.100
Hello. I got you a present.

00:42.101 --> 00:43.804
It's a thumb.

00:43.805 --> 00:44.972
Don't look away.

00:44.973 --> 00:46.776
Let the fear wash over you.

00:46.777 --> 00:48.111
I don't understand.

00:48.112 --> 00:49.614
That's the whole point.

00:49.615 --> 00:52.185
Now, did you leave a plate
of black coffee out for me?

00:52.186 --> 00:54.356
- No.
- In the future,

00:54.357 --> 00:57.428
please leave a plate of
black coffee out for me.

00:57.429 --> 00:59.565
Also in the past.

00:59.566 --> 01:02.036
You guys, what are you
doing watching TV?

01:02.037 --> 01:03.974
- It's snowing.
- Really?

01:03.975 --> 01:06.653
Wow, it's so beautiful!

01:06.654 --> 01:07.446
Isn't it?

01:07.447 --> 01:09.183
And you know what's a miracle, kids?

01:09.184 --> 01:12.723
Every single snowflake is exactly alike.

01:12.724 --> 01:14.192
I don't think that's right.

01:14.193 --> 01:16.463
No, it's true. Just like fingerprints.

01:16.464 --> 01:18.366
All right, you guys ready for church?

01:18.367 --> 01:19.861
Church? What are you, an idiot?

01:19.862 --> 01:21.237
It's the first snow of the season.

01:21.239 --> 01:22.239
We're going sledding.

01:22.240 --> 01:23.842
Please, can we, Mom?

01:23.843 --> 01:25.312
Well, I mean, it's Sunday, and...

01:25.313 --> 01:26.881
Come on, Lois. After all,

01:26.882 --> 01:29.350
sledding was the second
passion of the Christ.

01:29.654 --> 01:32.486
Eat this, for this is my dust!

01:37.000 --> 01:38.502
My sled has Dora on it

01:38.503 --> 01:40.773
'cause my parents got it at a yard sale.

01:40.774 --> 01:42.442
It's still for boys though.

01:42.443 --> 01:45.112
She's about language
acquisition, not gender.

01:46.918 --> 01:48.119
Sorry, fun-seekers,

01:48.120 --> 01:50.256
this hill is closed to sledding.

01:50.257 --> 01:51.659
What? What are you talking about?

01:51.660 --> 01:54.130
Too many pansy-ass parents sue the city

01:54.131 --> 01:55.566
when their kids sprain a finger

01:55.567 --> 01:57.536
or crush their skull on a bumper.

01:57.537 --> 02:00.742
I'm afraid sledding has
been banned in Quahog.

02:00.743 --> 02:02.979
You can't do that! Last time I checked,

02:02.980 --> 02:04.749
<i>this is still the United States of Tara.</i>

02:04.750 --> 02:05.851
Obscure reference.

02:05.852 --> 02:07.420
And I'm not gonna let anybody tell me

02:07.421 --> 02:09.191
where I can and cannot sled!

02:09.192 --> 02:10.793
Yeah, you're right.

02:10.794 --> 02:12.329
Power to the people!

02:12.330 --> 02:16.235
The whole world is watching!
The whole world is watching!

02:17.806 --> 02:19.409
What... what just happened?

02:19.410 --> 02:20.911
Who cares? Last one down the hill...

02:20.912 --> 02:22.914
Oh, my God!

02:22.915 --> 02:24.050
Call my mom!

02:24.051 --> 02:26.688
I crushed my skull on a bumper!

02:30.005 --> 02:32.766
You serious? All this white
stuff used to be water?

02:32.767 --> 02:34.736
Mm. My word.

02:34.737 --> 02:35.960
Joe, what are you riding on?

02:35.961 --> 02:38.376
Oh, it's a bedpan.
I got a ton of these at home.

02:38.377 --> 02:41.380
You make every activity incredibly sad.

02:44.655 --> 02:46.507
There you are. Where have you been?

02:46.509 --> 02:48.093
I just ran home to get the big sled

02:48.094 --> 02:49.228
out of our dining room.

02:49.229 --> 02:50.464
What are you talking about?

02:50.465 --> 02:52.001
We don't have a sled in our dining room.

02:52.002 --> 02:53.470
Everybody on!

02:53.471 --> 02:55.774
Peter, the dining room
table is an antique.

02:55.775 --> 02:57.973
It's been in my family
for six generations.

02:57.980 --> 02:58.981
It's fine.

02:58.982 --> 03:00.451
Okay, now, since we're white guys

03:00.452 --> 03:03.522
doing something stupid,
everybody grab a GoPro.

03:07.565 --> 03:09.233
Yeah, this is awesome!

03:09.234 --> 03:10.569
Oh, we're drifting.

03:10.570 --> 03:11.904
W-We're turning. We're turning!

03:11.905 --> 03:12.973
Dad, I'm scared.

03:12.974 --> 03:14.109
We're backwards!

03:14.110 --> 03:15.779
Am I the only one
who thinks that now

03:15.780 --> 03:18.149
we're at an alarming speed?

03:24.596 --> 03:26.264
Peter, are you insane?!

03:26.265 --> 03:28.234
You could have killed the entire family!

03:28.235 --> 03:31.073
Sorry, Lois. I honestly thought
this was gonna be fun.

03:31.074 --> 03:33.444
Like when I won that sex contest.

03:33.445 --> 03:34.578
First again!

03:34.579 --> 03:36.015
Wasn't even close, was it?

03:36.016 --> 03:38.385
No, Peter, it wasn't even close.

03:38.386 --> 03:39.955
Yeah, you are terrible at this.

03:39.956 --> 03:41.258
Now, why don't you clean up

03:41.259 --> 03:43.461
and go get the champ a Gatorade, huh?

03:48.739 --> 03:50.741
You wearing pants always amuses me.

03:50.742 --> 03:52.912
Yeah, I know. It's just
I got roped into going

03:52.913 --> 03:54.648
to some stupid office Christmas party

03:54.649 --> 03:56.118
with this girl I'm dating.

03:56.119 --> 03:57.520
Really? I thought you just went

03:57.521 --> 03:59.623
to an office Christmas
party with her last week.

03:59.624 --> 04:01.227
What? Oh, no, um...

04:01.228 --> 04:03.430
No, that-that was
this other girl I was dating.

04:03.431 --> 04:06.736
Um, her name was... Kow-ooch.

04:06.737 --> 04:09.174
Did you just say "couch,"
but pronounce it strangely

04:09.175 --> 04:10.710
so it sounded like a name?

04:10.711 --> 04:12.146
What's going on, Brian?

04:12.147 --> 04:13.816
All right, look,
I've been crashing

04:13.817 --> 04:15.786
office Christmas parties
for the free booze

04:15.787 --> 04:18.357
and drunk women who don't want
to spend the holidays alone.

04:18.358 --> 04:20.428
Oh, so you're a Christmas party creep.

04:20.429 --> 04:23.166
Just like the fat man is
a pool party creep.

04:23.167 --> 04:24.768
Now, Chris, you're getting older,

04:24.769 --> 04:27.741
so it's time for you to learn
the classic pool party game

04:27.742 --> 04:29.844
"Talk to Somebody's Wife in a Bikini

04:29.845 --> 04:31.848
Until They Cover Up Uncomfortably."

04:31.849 --> 04:33.417
So, Bonnie, how are things going?

04:33.418 --> 04:35.188
Oh, things are fine.

04:35.189 --> 04:38.493
Been kind of busy lately,
what with Susie starting to...

04:38.494 --> 04:40.230
Okay, bye.

04:40.231 --> 04:42.033
Man, that's, like, two seconds.

04:42.034 --> 04:44.638
Hey, Peter. Hey, what have you
been watching on TV lately?

04:44.639 --> 04:45.940
Oh, you know, this and that.

04:45.941 --> 04:47.644
<i>There's a show called Shipping Wars.</i>

04:47.645 --> 04:49.445
Uh, it's actually kinda... Okay, bye.

04:55.859 --> 04:58.195
Oh, boy, the Marshalls
is now a Nordstrom.

04:58.196 --> 05:00.366
I feel like our days at
this mall are numbered.

05:00.367 --> 05:01.835
Well, we have $60.

05:01.836 --> 05:04.340
Let's see what kind of
Chinese pressed-board garbage

05:04.341 --> 05:05.842
we can get to replace my grandmother's

05:05.843 --> 05:07.646
priceless mahogany table.

05:07.647 --> 05:09.582
Dad, look, Santa's here!

05:11.421 --> 05:13.122
I want to sit on his lap.

05:13.123 --> 05:14.858
Geez, Chris, come on.
You're in high school.

05:14.859 --> 05:17.163
I'm gonna ask him for
a family trampoline.

05:17.164 --> 05:19.300
Holy crap, get your ass up there!

05:19.301 --> 05:20.836
You know what, Peter?

05:20.837 --> 05:22.172
I'll get the table myself.

05:22.173 --> 05:24.009
And then I might just sit in that car

05:24.010 --> 05:26.278
in the middle of the mall and cry.

05:28.317 --> 05:29.885
Geez, look at this line.

05:29.886 --> 05:32.123
Yeah, no kidding. And it's not moving.

05:32.124 --> 05:35.028
Me and my adopted son have
been waiting quite a while.

05:35.029 --> 05:37.499
Wait, what... Why did you...

05:37.500 --> 05:38.868
I didn't even ask.

05:38.869 --> 05:40.972
So is your son a biolog?

05:40.973 --> 05:42.241
What... I'm not...

05:42.242 --> 05:44.712
<i>I-I don't watch Modern Family, sorry.</i>

05:44.713 --> 05:46.786
Hey, Chris, wait here.
I'm gonna see what's going on.

05:48.015 --> 05:49.688
Hey, Muscles, what's taking so long?

05:49.689 --> 05:51.825
I'm sorry, sir. This may shock you,

05:51.826 --> 05:53.928
but it turns out the
seasonal Santa we hired

05:53.929 --> 05:55.552
has a drinking problem.

05:55.553 --> 05:56.934
And I don't know where
to find a replacement

05:56.935 --> 05:58.504
on such short notice.

05:58.505 --> 06:00.608
Hey, you're a hefty guy.

06:00.609 --> 06:01.943
I called you "Muscles."

06:01.944 --> 06:03.413
Would you mind putting on the suit

06:03.414 --> 06:05.715
and playing Santa,
just until the shift ends?

06:05.717 --> 06:07.119
I'd pay you for your time.

06:07.121 --> 06:08.255
All right, fine.

06:08.256 --> 06:10.693
I mean, it's not the first time
I pretended to be someone else.

06:10.694 --> 06:11.895
I once dressed as a farmer

06:11.896 --> 06:14.305
to get a date on FarmersOnly.com.

06:14.600 --> 06:16.169
Are you Peter?

06:16.170 --> 06:17.938
Yeah. A-Are you the gross lady

06:17.939 --> 06:20.142
who lives in the
converted horse trailer?

06:20.143 --> 06:23.415
♪ You don't have to be lonely ♪

06:23.416 --> 06:26.922
♪ At FarmersOnly.com ♪

06:26.923 --> 06:30.627
It doesn't say "whites only,"
but... yeah.

06:39.345 --> 06:41.347
'Sup? Slammin' pantsuit.

06:41.348 --> 06:42.950
Hey, I'm Scott Fitzgerald.

06:42.951 --> 06:45.387
You probably don't recognize me
'cause I'm in corporate.

06:45.388 --> 06:47.525
<i>So am I. This is corporate.</i>

06:47.526 --> 06:50.463
A little
too much so, if you ask me.

06:50.464 --> 06:52.501
I... I try to have fun, right?

06:52.502 --> 06:54.926
I-I mean, we're not,
we're not landing planes here.

06:54.927 --> 06:58.109
Our company manufactures
aircraft landing gear systems.

06:58.110 --> 06:59.412
Yep, uh-huh.

06:59.413 --> 07:03.019
Well, I am going to fly us over
a few more drinks.

07:04.924 --> 07:06.492
Stewie? What are you doing here?

07:06.493 --> 07:08.496
I followed you. I had to see for myself

07:08.497 --> 07:10.699
just how desperate and
pathetic you really are.

07:10.700 --> 07:12.270
And don't worry, I'm not sticking around

07:12.271 --> 07:13.338
this sad little... Ooh!

07:13.339 --> 07:15.273
Is that rolled-up ham for everyone?

07:15.275 --> 07:16.910
Yeah. Okay.

07:16.912 --> 07:18.347
Well, I'll see you at home...

07:18.348 --> 07:20.717
Hey, everyone,
karaoke's starting!

07:20.718 --> 07:22.354
Well, I could watch and make fun

07:22.355 --> 07:23.824
for just a few... Oh, my God!

07:23.825 --> 07:25.626
They have a photo booth
with funny props!

07:25.627 --> 07:27.997
Oh, I call the big funny glasses!

07:38.985 --> 07:41.455
And I want a tricycle and a pony

07:41.456 --> 07:43.024
and an American Girl doll

07:43.025 --> 07:45.462
and a drone with a camera
and a gun that fires...

07:45.463 --> 07:47.765
Ho, ho, ho. Yeah, sure, all of it.

07:48.803 --> 07:50.471
All right, now, go pick up your picture.

07:50.472 --> 07:51.974
And before you go crying to your mom,

07:51.975 --> 07:53.877
that's my cell phone you're feeling.

07:55.915 --> 07:58.352
Hey, Santa Claus, you going home soon?

07:58.353 --> 08:00.522
Well, depending on how traffic is

08:00.523 --> 08:02.393
at the North Pole.

08:02.394 --> 08:03.829
So what can I get for you today?

08:03.830 --> 08:05.198
Milk and cookies?

08:05.199 --> 08:06.600
Oh, okay.

08:06.601 --> 08:07.702
Sorry I started this.

08:07.703 --> 08:09.071
Chicken burrito, please.

08:09.072 --> 08:11.342
There you go. Merry Christmas.

08:11.343 --> 08:12.544
Uh, how much do I, uh...

08:12.545 --> 08:14.714
Oh, come on, I'm not
charging Santa Claus.

08:14.715 --> 08:15.783
It's on the house.

08:15.784 --> 08:16.927
This is free because

08:16.929 --> 08:18.421
I'm dressed as Santa?

08:18.422 --> 08:20.625
That's right. Anything for Santa.

08:20.626 --> 08:21.661
Anything?

08:21.662 --> 08:23.430
Holy crap, this is awesome!

08:23.431 --> 08:24.732
I'm Santa Claus.

08:24.733 --> 08:26.802
In this suit I'm like a god.

08:31.880 --> 08:33.426
I got a free burrito!

08:40.177 --> 08:42.327
Ugh, look at these two lumps.

08:42.329 --> 08:44.633
♪ Up on the housetop
click, click, click ♪

08:44.635 --> 08:46.738
♪ Slipped on the chimney
and broke his... ♪

08:46.739 --> 08:47.873
Mornin'. ♪ Penis ♪

08:47.874 --> 08:50.712
Dad, why are you still
wearing that Santa suit?

08:50.713 --> 08:52.081
Well, the guy at the mall asked me

08:52.082 --> 08:53.918
to stay on till Christmas,
and I said yes,

08:53.919 --> 08:55.253
'cause being Santa's awesome.

08:55.254 --> 08:57.357
You wear this suit,
it's like a free pass.

08:57.358 --> 08:58.860
People let you do anything you want.

08:58.861 --> 09:00.262
What are you talking about?

09:00.264 --> 09:02.350
Oh, it's the stuff of dreams, Lois.

09:02.352 --> 09:05.406
Free burritos, free orange
chicken, free pretzels.

09:05.408 --> 09:06.974
Did you make it out of the food court?

09:06.975 --> 09:08.143
I made it to the border.

09:08.144 --> 09:10.647
I got a free iPhone case
and a tiny license plate.

09:10.648 --> 09:11.950
It says "Corey."

09:11.951 --> 09:14.321
Yep. Cost me zilch.

09:19.498 --> 09:21.667
So, who's this "Mary Christmas"

09:21.668 --> 09:23.103
everybody keeps talking about?

09:23.104 --> 09:24.873
Oh...

09:24.874 --> 09:26.877
that's very clever.

09:26.878 --> 09:28.079
I don't recognize you.

09:28.080 --> 09:29.548
Which department are you in?

09:29.549 --> 09:32.052
Well, right now I'm in Boob Assessment.

09:32.053 --> 09:33.355
Eww.

09:33.356 --> 09:35.696
Hey, you were right about
office Christmas parties.

09:35.698 --> 09:37.367
- They're fantastic!
- Uh-huh, okay.

09:37.369 --> 09:38.804
I'm gonna keep looking around the room

09:38.806 --> 09:39.840
while you talk.

09:39.842 --> 09:41.612
Yes, it's like watching a soap opera,

09:41.613 --> 09:43.248
what with all the drunken misbehavior

09:43.249 --> 09:44.650
and ill-advised hookups.

09:44.651 --> 09:46.606
And down the hall they're
doing a "white elephant."

09:46.608 --> 09:47.874
Oh, that gift-exchange thing?

09:47.875 --> 09:50.579
No, there's a fat secretary
taking on all comers.

09:50.580 --> 09:52.950
Where, uh, uh, which office is that in?

09:52.951 --> 09:54.352
Oh, you won't miss her.
She's still wearing

09:54.353 --> 09:55.721
the felt antlers.

09:55.722 --> 09:57.790
Absolute freak show in there.

09:58.994 --> 10:00.463
Hey, what the hell's going on?

10:00.464 --> 10:02.133
Oh, Santa. I-I'm sorry.

10:02.134 --> 10:03.468
I didn't realize this was your car.

10:03.469 --> 10:05.572
That's right. Now,
crumple up that ticket.

10:06.943 --> 10:08.215
Now eat it!

10:09.414 --> 10:11.115
All right, now we're
gonna go to your home

10:11.116 --> 10:12.351
and wait for you to pass it,

10:12.352 --> 10:14.154
and then you're gonna eat it again.

10:14.155 --> 10:16.258
Hey, honey, this is Santa.

10:16.259 --> 10:17.894
He's gonna come in
and watch me in the bathroom.

10:17.895 --> 10:19.297
Oh, just like the Easter Bunny did.

10:19.298 --> 10:20.566
Exactly.

10:20.567 --> 10:22.802
I got a lot of guys coming through here.

10:25.141 --> 10:26.710
The next composition is

10:26.711 --> 10:29.549
<i>Opus Dei, Dei Dei Pater,</i>

10:29.550 --> 10:31.986
seventh movement, by Chopin.

10:35.426 --> 10:38.523
Correction. The next composition

10:38.525 --> 10:42.528
is 1-877-Kars-4-Kids.

10:45.044 --> 10:49.017
♪ 1-877-Kars-4-Kids ♪

10:49.018 --> 10:52.723
♪ K-A-R-S Kars-4-Kids ♪

10:52.724 --> 10:56.096
♪ 1-877-Kars-4-Kids ♪

10:56.097 --> 10:59.903
♪ Donate your car today... ♪

11:00.770 --> 11:03.057
I lost my virginity to this song.

11:08.930 --> 11:10.298
Ugh, this party's a dud.

11:10.300 --> 11:11.190
Yeah, no kidding.

11:11.191 --> 11:13.060
That lady turned off a Hall & Oates song

11:13.061 --> 11:14.797
because it was "too provocative."

11:14.798 --> 11:16.166
Everyone, let's remember,

11:16.167 --> 11:17.702
this is still a workplace.

11:17.703 --> 11:18.837
Sorry, Barb.

11:18.838 --> 11:20.440
You know what? I got an idea.

11:20.441 --> 11:24.013
I'm gonna stir up some drama,
make this party interesting.

11:25.450 --> 11:28.252
Excuse me? Uh, could I have
your attention please? Hi.

11:28.288 --> 11:30.926
Hi, I'm Chadwick Redmayne
from the regional office.

11:30.927 --> 11:33.497
Unfortunately, since people
only use printers now

11:33.498 --> 11:35.968
to print out boarding passes
for their grandparents,

11:35.969 --> 11:38.973
40% of you will
be laid off as of Monday.

11:38.974 --> 11:41.811
Oh, and whoever drinks
the most shots keeps their job.

11:45.920 --> 11:48.691
See? That's how you get a party started.

11:48.692 --> 11:50.727
Mr. Redmayne, I don't know who you are,

11:50.728 --> 11:53.198
but I've been in charge of
this office for 16 years...

11:53.199 --> 11:55.102
- Sad.
- And I want to thank you.

11:55.103 --> 11:57.172
I've been trying to reduce
our staff costs for months,

11:57.173 --> 11:59.042
but just didn't have the guts to do it,

11:59.043 --> 12:00.411
much less before Christmas.

12:00.412 --> 12:02.949
Yeah, well, that's why
they send in Channing Redwick,

12:02.950 --> 12:05.020
or Chadmayne, or whatever,

12:05.021 --> 12:06.456
I don't even remember what I said.

12:06.457 --> 12:08.392
We could use someone
like you around here.

12:08.393 --> 12:10.804
Welcome aboard. See you Monday.

12:11.666 --> 12:13.702
Wow, a paying, grown-up job!

12:13.703 --> 12:15.372
I haven't been this excited
about anything

12:15.373 --> 12:17.976
<i>since the night Wicked
premiered in Quahog.</i>

12:17.977 --> 12:20.415
All right, Brian,
let's rob these gay guys.

12:20.417 --> 12:21.316
What if they're home?

12:21.317 --> 12:22.769
They're not gonna be home.

12:26.193 --> 12:28.395
Bye, Santa!

12:28.396 --> 12:29.898
Bye, strippers!

12:29.899 --> 12:32.168
Uh, you can all take
your clothes off now,

12:32.169 --> 12:34.171
I was just comin' in for the spaghetti.

12:37.278 --> 12:38.747
Aah! Bitch!

12:38.748 --> 12:40.283
Ah, that hurts.

12:40.284 --> 12:42.353
Ah, I'm drunk.

12:42.354 --> 12:43.822
Heart's beatin' fast.

12:48.065 --> 12:50.134
Spaghetti angel!

12:50.135 --> 12:52.706
I'm makin' a spaghetti angel.

12:52.707 --> 12:54.876
When Italian guys die, they...

12:54.877 --> 12:56.446
they turn into...

12:56.447 --> 12:57.581
into...

12:57.582 --> 13:00.719
into...

13:01.923 --> 13:03.091
Peter.

13:03.092 --> 13:05.561
Peter Griffin.

13:06.565 --> 13:09.335
Peter? We need to talk.

13:09.336 --> 13:11.138
Who... Who are you?

13:11.139 --> 13:13.342
I'm the real Santa Claus.

13:13.343 --> 13:16.916
Awesome! Okay, my first wish
is for a thousand wishes.

13:16.917 --> 13:18.986
- Yes!
- That's not me. That's a genie.

13:18.987 --> 13:21.524
Okay, then my first wish is for a genie.

13:21.525 --> 13:23.227
Again, you'd need a genie.

13:23.228 --> 13:24.392
How wasted are you?

13:24.394 --> 13:25.618
Don't judge me.

13:25.620 --> 13:26.931
You live in a bottle.

13:26.933 --> 13:28.924
It's a lamp. And I'm not a genie!

13:34.454 --> 13:35.789
All right, come on now, pal, seriously,

13:35.790 --> 13:36.958
who are you really?

13:36.959 --> 13:39.272
I already told you, I'm Santa Claus.

13:39.274 --> 13:40.096
Oh, yeah?

13:40.097 --> 13:42.100
Well, if you're Santa,
then what did I ask for

13:42.101 --> 13:44.471
- for Christmas when I was 12?
- Nothing.

13:44.472 --> 13:45.974
<i>Because it was the year
you found that Penthouse</i>

13:45.975 --> 13:46.976
in the woods.

13:46.977 --> 13:49.213
You really are Santa!

13:49.214 --> 13:51.049
Am I really heavier than you?

13:51.050 --> 13:53.254
I-I got to, I got to take control.

13:53.255 --> 13:55.324
Look, I'm not very happy with you.

13:55.325 --> 13:57.561
You can't go around in that suit
pretending you're me

13:57.562 --> 13:59.398
and acting like a complete jackass.

13:59.399 --> 14:01.067
What are you talking about?
People love me.

14:01.068 --> 14:02.370
They give me free stuff.

14:02.371 --> 14:04.072
<i>No, they love me.</i>

14:04.073 --> 14:06.410
You're just exploiting
my brand for personal gain

14:06.411 --> 14:08.314
and destroying my reputation.

14:08.315 --> 14:09.917
So there's, like, no
toilet on the sleigh,

14:09.918 --> 14:11.319
so you're, you're just,

14:11.320 --> 14:13.123
you're just crapping in
people's houses, right?

14:13.124 --> 14:14.124
You're not hearing me.

14:14.125 --> 14:16.395
Stop wearing that suit, or else.

14:16.396 --> 14:17.864
Or else what?

14:17.865 --> 14:22.272
Or else I will put you
at the top of my naughty list.

14:22.273 --> 14:24.376
You know, you're not talking
to a little kid anymore,

14:24.377 --> 14:26.046
so get the hell out of my face, Santa.

14:26.047 --> 14:28.050
I like this suit, and I'm keeping it.

14:28.051 --> 14:29.319
Now, if you'll excuse me,

14:29.320 --> 14:31.455
you're standing in my
strip club spaghetti.

14:31.456 --> 14:33.859
I got to get this home
to my family for supper.

14:38.569 --> 14:40.471
You better watch out.

14:51.960 --> 14:53.295
Gail?

14:53.296 --> 14:54.964
Gail, is your Internet working?

14:54.965 --> 14:55.966
Mine's slow.

14:59.707 --> 15:01.509
Oh, my God, Gail, what happened?

15:01.510 --> 15:04.815
I just found out I'm part
of the downsizing you announced.

15:04.816 --> 15:05.844
Oh, no.

15:06.219 --> 15:08.154
So your Internet, is it...

15:08.155 --> 15:09.423
is it slow?

15:09.424 --> 15:12.329
Gail, you were supposed
to be gone an hour ago.

15:12.330 --> 15:13.531
Hey, give her a break, man.

15:13.532 --> 15:15.401
This is Gail Devereaux-Slansky.

15:15.402 --> 15:17.905
Oh, it's just Gail Devereaux now.

15:17.906 --> 15:19.441
Oof. Tough week.

15:19.442 --> 15:20.945
Why don't you stop rubbernecking

15:20.946 --> 15:23.549
and finish that
payroll report I asked for?

15:23.550 --> 15:25.652
I can't believe I got fired.

15:25.653 --> 15:28.023
And right before the holidays.

15:28.024 --> 15:30.094
Oh, God, I've ruined Christmas.

15:30.095 --> 15:33.767
Like the Little Drummer Boy when
he got really into Neil Peart.

15:36.039 --> 15:39.210
♪ Our finest gifts we bring ♪

15:39.211 --> 15:42.048
♪ Pa-rum-pum-pum-pum ♪

16:00.783 --> 16:02.697
Christmas is gonna be sick!

16:07.496 --> 16:09.899
So, Dad, now that you made Santa mad,

16:09.900 --> 16:12.270
aren't you scared he's gonna
do something bad to you?

16:12.271 --> 16:13.505
Ah, Santa's all talk.

16:13.506 --> 16:14.573
He ain't gonna do nothing.

16:17.279 --> 16:18.313
Hey, Peter.

16:18.314 --> 16:19.850
Ready to go to Build-A-Bear?

16:19.851 --> 16:21.353
What? What are you talking about?

16:21.354 --> 16:22.355
I got your text.

16:22.356 --> 16:24.425
It says, "Hey, Joe, cancel your plans.

16:24.426 --> 16:26.529
Let's go to Build-A-Bear."
I didn't send you a...

16:26.530 --> 16:28.666
Oh, son of a bitch, Santa.

16:28.667 --> 16:30.402
Joe, I did not send you a text.

16:30.403 --> 16:32.740
Well, you sent another text that says,

16:32.741 --> 16:36.246
"Hey, Joe, it's definitely me,
Peter, who sent the text."

16:36.247 --> 16:38.851
Damn it, he covered all bases.

16:38.852 --> 16:39.885
What do you think, Peter?

16:39.886 --> 16:41.956
Maybe a little sun hat for Cindy?

16:41.957 --> 16:44.194
Whatever, I'm done with my bear.
Let's get out of here.

16:44.195 --> 16:46.832
Well, the text you sent
earlier would disagree.

16:46.833 --> 16:48.936
You said, "No matter what I say,

16:48.937 --> 16:50.972
I want to build multiple bears."

16:50.973 --> 16:53.343
Joe, I swear to you,
I do not want to do that.

16:54.413 --> 16:57.717
News flash, Peter, looks like you do.

17:00.757 --> 17:03.863
Would anyone like to lead
the family in a holiday prayer?

17:03.864 --> 17:06.634
I'll tell you who should be
saying his prayers, Santa.

17:06.635 --> 17:08.604
He messes with me, I mess with him.

17:08.605 --> 17:10.908
That's why I replaced
one of his flying reindeer

17:10.909 --> 17:13.412
with an ordinary, non-magical one.

17:16.520 --> 17:18.188
Cut it off, cut it off!

17:22.964 --> 17:25.334
You know, I think this year
is gonna be the best...

17:27.005 --> 17:29.340
Yay, free horse!

17:39.394 --> 17:40.395
What the hell?

17:40.396 --> 17:42.364
Hey, Chris, get in here.

17:42.365 --> 17:43.867
This is impossible, right?

17:43.868 --> 17:45.837
All of Meg's farts here in this box?

17:45.838 --> 17:47.307
I would think that's impossible.

17:47.308 --> 17:49.109
Yeah, right? That's impossible.

17:51.081 --> 17:53.050
Is this the box? Yeah, that's it.

17:55.590 --> 17:57.391
Yeah, that's impossible.
I know, it's impossible.

17:57.392 --> 17:59.095
Right... O-okay, all right,
I'm opening it.

17:59.096 --> 18:01.866
Unless whoever sent it was magic.

18:01.867 --> 18:04.570
Oh, well, now that's interesting.

18:08.946 --> 18:10.782
Chad, we got to talk about this report.

18:10.783 --> 18:12.785
Why do you write all
your twos backwards?

18:12.786 --> 18:14.689
Well, you know it's a two,
so why are we talking?

18:14.690 --> 18:17.227
Fix it, or you're fired.

18:17.228 --> 18:18.263
You know what?

18:18.264 --> 18:19.632
I thought working in a cubicle

18:19.633 --> 18:21.301
at a mid-sized printing company

18:21.302 --> 18:23.171
would be the adventure of a lifetime.

18:23.172 --> 18:25.776
Instead, it's been nothing
but tedium and cruelty.

18:25.777 --> 18:28.180
It's time to set things right.

18:28.181 --> 18:29.683
Here you go, Warren.

18:29.684 --> 18:31.019
Merry Christmas.

18:31.020 --> 18:32.655
$11,000?

18:32.656 --> 18:35.560
Yes, it's the maximum check
amount I'm authorized to cut.

18:35.561 --> 18:37.397
Cash it fast.

18:37.398 --> 18:41.270
Merry Christmas, cash it fast.
Merry Christmas, cash it fast.

18:41.271 --> 18:42.906
Merry Christmas, cash it fast.

18:42.907 --> 18:44.910
Thanks, Chadwick. This is awesome.

18:44.911 --> 18:47.314
I think you mean "Happy Holidays."

18:53.059 --> 18:55.094
You got to be kidding me.

18:57.934 --> 19:00.537
Oh, this is too good.

19:05.281 --> 19:06.349
Point, Griffin.

19:06.350 --> 19:07.651
Let's see you top...

19:09.154 --> 19:10.289
Now you gonna listen?

19:10.290 --> 19:11.491
Now you gonna listen, you little bitch?

19:11.492 --> 19:13.261
- Whose suit are you wearing?
- Your suit!

19:13.262 --> 19:14.697
- Whose suit?
- Your suit!

19:14.698 --> 19:15.766
It's your suit!

19:19.106 --> 19:20.407
Okay, okay,

19:20.408 --> 19:22.211
I'll never wear that Santa suit again.

19:22.212 --> 19:25.282
Just stop terrorizing me and
take me off the naughty list.

19:25.283 --> 19:26.852
- You promise?
- Yes!

19:27.929 --> 19:29.123
Thank you.

19:29.124 --> 19:32.796
I've always known you were
a good boy deep inside, Peter.

19:32.797 --> 19:35.300
And just so you know
there are no hard feelings,

19:35.301 --> 19:37.371
this is for you.

19:37.372 --> 19:39.876
<i>It's that Penthouse
you found in the woods.</i>

19:39.877 --> 19:43.549
With Vanessa Williams
and George Burns on the cover?

19:43.550 --> 19:44.684
I'm glad you like it.

19:44.685 --> 19:46.187
I had to buy it from a really creepy guy

19:46.188 --> 19:47.389
on the Internet.

19:47.850 --> 19:50.761
Look, Santa, I owe you an apology.

19:50.762 --> 19:53.299
I'm sorry I took
advantage of your good name.

19:53.300 --> 19:56.806
You spread so much joy and
wonder to kids everywhere,

19:56.807 --> 19:59.739
and I just used that
to get stuff for myself.

20:00.246 --> 20:01.781
Apology accepted.

20:01.782 --> 20:03.718
And truth is,

20:03.719 --> 20:05.121
you weren't the worst Santa.

20:05.122 --> 20:07.291
This was the worst Santa.

20:09.496 --> 20:10.964
Oh, ho, ho, ho!

20:10.965 --> 20:12.267
Oh, and that's another thing.

20:12.268 --> 20:13.803
<i>It's "Ho, ho, ho."</i>

20:13.804 --> 20:15.306
Everybody pronounces it wrong.

20:15.307 --> 20:16.608
It's very irritating.

20:21.351 --> 20:22.619
So long, Peter.

20:22.620 --> 20:24.923
Glad to have you back on the nice list.

20:33.539 --> 20:35.809
Merry Christmas!

20:35.810 --> 20:37.812
<i>Ho, ho, ho.</i>

20:42.956 --> 20:46.328
<i>And that was the
Christmas I would never forget.</i>

20:46.329 --> 20:50.402
<i>Until I went home and had,
like, 50 beers, and did forget.</i>

20:50.403 --> 20:53.040
<i>But only after I screamed
myself into a blackout</i>

20:53.041 --> 20:55.378
<i>while my whole family held me down.</i>

20:55.379 --> 20:56.849
<i>Merry Christmas.</i>

20:56.850 --> 20:59.043
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru